From a97ef39773a436cb7d390ab402e569a9cf1de000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 13:48:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 004/638] net: add native AROSTCP socket and resolver support
 [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-bringup

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: Chromium net calls POSIX socket and resolver APIs directly, while AROS requires a valid per-task bsdsocket.library base and exposes several interfaces through library vectors rather than libc declarations.

FIX_REASON: Centralize AROSTCP lifecycle and calls in the base socket adapter, then route DNS, interfaces, TCP/UDP options, and error translation through it. WebSocket's source-local List-style collision is removed without altering protocol behavior.

SCOPE: net build selection, AROS network-interface and DNS-config services, resolver paths, socket descriptors/options, TCP/UDP operations, and WebSocket inflater naming.

VALIDATION: focused net and WebSocket objects compile and the full headless graph progressed through generated Mojo/net consumers into Skia.

RISK: medium; network-change notification and richer host configuration remain limited by the currently exposed AROSTCP APIs.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
